1
00:00:29,980 --> 00:00:32,420
Here we go! Everybody, don't move!

2
00:00:32,820 --> 00:00:34,330
This is definitely reckless.

3
00:00:34,380 --> 00:00:37,500
Making a senior officer play the
criminal in a crime prevention drill...

4
00:00:37,960 --> 00:00:40,889
It can't be helped.
I strongly opposed it too, but

5
00:00:40,939 --> 00:00:44,460
headquarters' computer
went and picked Ryotsu.

6
00:00:45,120 --> 00:00:48,460
Ryo-chan was unusually fired up,
but I'm worried.

7
00:00:48,840 --> 00:00:52,400
Since Terai-san is with him,
I don't think he'll go wild.

8
00:00:53,280 --> 00:00:55,623
It's only a drill, after all.

9
00:00:55,673 --> 00:00:58,580
If we follow the manual,
there won't be any problems...

10
00:01:02,020 --> 00:01:03,740
If you move, you'll fall down hard.

11
00:01:05,760 --> 00:01:07,900
Ryo-san, you're going a bit overboard.

12
00:01:07,900 --> 00:01:10,860
If we don't go this far,
it won't be real training.

13
00:01:13,200 --> 00:01:14,200
Don't worry.

14
00:01:14,200 --> 00:01:17,500
All the pistols Ryo and the
others are holding are blanks.

15
00:01:18,060 --> 00:01:19,940
Is the alarm bell going off again?

16
00:01:19,940 --> 00:01:21,600
It's about to ring.

17
00:01:21,600 --> 00:01:23,620
Once it does, we'll dispatch immediately.

18
00:01:26,420 --> 00:01:27,080
Whoops

19
00:01:27,080 --> 00:01:31,020
Hold on! If you move like that, you'll
figure out there's an alarm bell right there!

20
00:01:32,980 --> 00:01:33,980
There, see!

21
00:01:34,760 --> 00:01:37,460
Ryo-san, at this rate nobody
will be able to report it!

22
00:01:37,600 --> 00:01:40,560
What are you talking about! Just because
it's training doesn't mean I'll go easy!

23
00:01:41,420 --> 00:01:44,400
The alarm isn't ringing! What's going on?

24
00:01:44,740 --> 00:01:46,060
Chief, the monitor!

25
00:01:46,280 --> 00:01:46,820
What happened?

26
00:01:47,160 --> 00:01:47,740
Whoaaa!

27
00:01:48,580 --> 00:01:50,680
With this,
you can't tell how close we are, right!

28
00:01:51,180 --> 00:01:52,940
This is bad, Ryo-san! You can't do that!

29
00:01:53,420 --> 00:01:54,020
You're naive!

30
00:01:54,460 --> 00:01:56,900
A robber today would do at least this much,
obviously.

31
00:01:56,900 --> 00:01:58,760
R-Ryotsu, that guy...

32
00:01:59,940 --> 00:02:01,000
Hand over the safe.

33
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:03,420
W-wait, isn't this fake money?

34
00:02:03,420 --> 00:02:05,060
That's exactly why it's fake money.

35
00:02:05,060 --> 00:02:07,280
We have to plan for every
possible situation, so

36
00:02:07,660 --> 00:02:08,700
Hurry up and hand it over.

37
00:02:08,700 --> 00:02:09,120
Yes.

38
00:02:10,080 --> 00:02:11,460
Hand the stack of bills over here.

39
00:02:11,460 --> 00:02:14,480
Good, now hand over
the dummy stack of bills.

40
00:02:14,880 --> 00:02:16,040
Dummy stack of bills?

41
00:02:16,440 --> 00:02:17,680
The moment you squeeze it tightly,

42
00:02:17,680 --> 00:02:20,220
it's rigged so the
electricity inside bursts out.

43
00:02:20,820 --> 00:02:21,460
We've been had.

44
00:02:21,860 --> 00:02:22,920
He fell for it.

45
00:02:24,020 --> 00:02:27,100
No good! At this rate,
we'll get caught no matter where we go!

46
00:02:28,440 --> 00:02:30,500
Quick, get the real tab in the slot!

47
00:02:30,500 --> 00:02:33,540
But that's just how the drill is!

48
00:02:33,700 --> 00:02:34,700
That's not allowed, Ryo-san!

49
00:02:35,220 --> 00:02:38,560
Idiot! If the money isn't really taken,
it won't feel realistic!

50
00:02:39,260 --> 00:02:42,320
Who's the idiot here! We can't
just sit around! Dispatch right now!

51
00:02:42,660 --> 00:02:45,600
We're dispatching without any report?

52
00:02:45,860 --> 00:02:48,060
If we let that idiot keep going like this,

53
00:02:48,110 --> 00:02:50,360
the police will lose all face!

54
00:02:50,920 --> 00:02:52,060
There's the patrol car.

55
00:02:56,980 --> 00:02:59,180
But without any report, how could

56
00:02:59,180 --> 00:03:01,040
Typical of Katsushika Station!

57
00:03:01,040 --> 00:03:03,020
Ryo-chan's running away!

58
00:03:03,980 --> 00:03:05,740
Hey, wait, Ryotsu!

59
00:03:05,740 --> 00:03:07,360
Chief!

60
00:03:08,100 --> 00:03:10,120
What do you think you're doing?

61
00:03:10,120 --> 00:03:10,840
Sorry.

62
00:03:11,560 --> 00:03:12,940
Chief, it's serious!

63
00:03:13,380 --> 00:03:16,100
There's a robbery at the
Kameari Bank just ahead, too,

64
00:03:16,100 --> 00:03:17,480
What?!

65
00:03:20,180 --> 00:03:21,480
Don't come any closer!

66
00:03:21,480 --> 00:03:24,860
Come near me and I'll blow
up the hostage with this bomb!

67
00:03:24,860 --> 00:03:26,100
Damn it.

68
00:03:32,320 --> 00:03:34,460
Don't tell me they're
running a drill here too.

69
00:03:34,460 --> 00:03:38,260
Senpai, no! Those guys are the real robbers!

70
00:03:38,260 --> 00:03:38,660
What?

71
00:03:40,320 --> 00:03:41,620
Whatever this is about,

72
00:03:41,620 --> 00:03:44,480
if you don't drop your guns,
the hostage's life is on the line!

73
00:03:49,660 --> 00:03:50,460
Let's go.

74
00:03:51,480 --> 00:03:52,640
Hey! Are we going in?!

75
00:03:53,660 --> 00:03:54,500
What?!

76
00:04:05,460 --> 00:04:09,080
Bang! This is also a blank for training!

77
00:04:09,200 --> 00:04:10,780
Suspect secured!

78
00:04:12,720 --> 00:04:13,680
Ryo-san!

79
00:04:13,920 --> 00:04:16,660
Chief! We've successfully
arrested the suspect!

80
00:04:17,480 --> 00:04:20,540
What are you saying!
Where did you get something like that?

81
00:04:21,480 --> 00:04:22,880
We just confiscated it, didn't we?

82
00:04:22,880 --> 00:04:25,720
Well, the criminal role needs some realism,
you know.

83
00:04:25,720 --> 00:04:26,840
Idiot!

84
00:04:26,840 --> 00:04:28,360
We don't need anything like that.

85
00:04:28,360 --> 00:04:30,720
After all the trouble I
went to preparing everything.

86
00:04:31,780 --> 00:04:32,820
Well then.

87
00:04:32,820 --> 00:04:34,140
Don't "well then" me!

88
00:04:34,580 --> 00:04:36,860
Return the stolen money at once.

89
00:04:37,780 --> 00:04:38,660
Come on.

90
00:04:38,660 --> 00:04:41,460
As if I'd actually steal it, right?

91
00:04:41,460 --> 00:04:41,940
Here.

92
00:04:43,960 --> 00:04:45,640
And the ones in your back pocket too.

93
00:04:47,540 --> 00:04:48,580
Right here, in a place like this?

94
00:04:48,580 --> 00:04:50,180
I wonder why it got mixed in.

95
00:04:52,560 --> 00:04:55,440
Here too, here too, here too

96
00:04:56,680 --> 00:05:00,280
This is bad!
The bomb's dimensional device is running!

97
00:05:00,460 --> 00:05:01,260
What!?

98
00:05:01,700 --> 00:05:03,280
It's going to explode in five minutes!

99
00:05:03,820 --> 00:05:06,860
Why would you use a
dimensional bomb to rob a bank!

100
00:05:07,120 --> 00:05:08,460
What an idiot!

101
00:05:08,700 --> 00:05:11,200
With this kind of thing,
if you just connect the timer's cord...

102
00:05:11,200 --> 00:05:12,120
Whoa!

103
00:05:12,700 --> 00:05:15,900
What's with all these cords!
There are way too many for the main unit!

104
00:05:16,020 --> 00:05:16,860
Seriously, how careless!

105
00:05:18,440 --> 00:05:20,820
Chief! Please do something!

106
00:05:23,120 --> 00:05:25,380
If it explodes here, it'll be a disaster!

107
00:05:25,380 --> 00:05:27,620
Senpai, let's go somewhere safe!

108
00:05:27,620 --> 00:05:29,120
Easier said than done!

109
00:05:29,760 --> 00:05:31,340
Hurry up, Ryotsu!

110
00:05:31,340 --> 00:05:34,240
Let's see, this goes here,
and that connects to this...

111
00:05:38,280 --> 00:05:39,300
You idiot!

112
00:05:39,300 --> 00:05:41,360
Sorry, let me borrow this bus!

113
00:05:41,360 --> 00:05:42,400
What?

114
00:05:42,400 --> 00:05:45,060
This dimensional bomb is going to explode!

115
00:05:45,060 --> 00:05:51,100
You too, get off quickly!

116
00:05:52,480 --> 00:05:53,220
That's my bus!

117
00:05:53,700 --> 00:05:55,730
Twenty years of service,
I'd sooner abandon my wife and kids,

118
00:05:55,780 --> 00:05:57,860
I can't let go of this bus!

119
00:05:58,020 --> 00:06:00,000
Don't blame me if you regret it!

120
00:06:04,760 --> 00:06:07,380
Do you have any idea how fast you were going,
you idiot?

121
00:06:07,380 --> 00:06:10,480
S-sorry, I was in a hurry.

122
00:06:10,480 --> 00:06:13,300
"Sorry"? If sorry were enough,
we wouldn't need the police!

123
00:06:13,840 --> 00:06:18,280
Be careful! If you cause an accident,
it'll be a disaster.

124
00:06:31,520 --> 00:06:32,920
Hurry! We don't have time!

125
00:06:33,400 --> 00:06:34,180
Watch out!

126
00:06:42,700 --> 00:06:43,900
Sorry!

127
00:06:47,200 --> 00:06:47,840
Nyah-nyah!

128
00:06:52,160 --> 00:06:52,940
It stopped!

129
00:06:53,100 --> 00:06:54,720
Damn it! We were so close!

130
00:06:54,980 --> 00:06:56,640
The routine was the problem after all!

131
00:06:57,500 --> 00:06:59,140
Honda! Perfect timing!

132
00:06:59,940 --> 00:07:02,380
This bomb goes off in one minute!

133
00:07:05,140 --> 00:07:05,840
Let's do this!

134
00:07:14,640 --> 00:07:17,400
Aaaaaah!

135
00:07:17,400 --> 00:07:19,320
This time it's really going to stop.

136
00:07:19,320 --> 00:07:20,320
Wait! Come here!

137
00:07:21,140 --> 00:07:22,480
This is no time for that!

138
00:07:22,840 --> 00:07:23,860
This way, right!

139
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:25,040
This way, right!

140
00:07:25,460 --> 00:07:26,280
With this...

141
00:07:26,280 --> 00:07:27,300
Here it comes!

142
00:07:31,120 --> 00:07:32,500
It's no use!

143
00:08:03,280 --> 00:08:04,700
Idiot!

144
00:08:04,700 --> 00:08:09,080
How can the damage caused by
the bus be worse than a bomb?

145
00:08:09,080 --> 00:08:11,520
It couldn't be helped, given the situation.

146
00:08:11,520 --> 00:08:15,480
Shut up! You're always,
always like this, you know that?

147
00:08:18,120 --> 00:08:18,880
Hey, Ryotsu!

148
00:08:19,020 --> 00:08:20,520
See you later!

149
00:08:21,080 --> 00:08:23,580
Hey! We're not done talking yet!

150
00:08:27,260 --> 00:08:30,180
It's probably best if he doesn't
return to the police box for a while.

151
00:08:30,600 --> 00:08:33,720
Well, the weather's nice, so he's just
out walking, pretending it's cycling?

152
00:08:34,880 --> 00:08:36,940
Ryotsu! Kankichi!

153
00:08:37,160 --> 00:08:38,220
Komachi and Naoko!

154
00:08:38,840 --> 00:08:40,700
I heard he caused another incident.

155
00:08:40,900 --> 00:08:42,940
Honestly,
he never does anything decent, does he?

156
00:08:43,420 --> 00:08:45,620
Shut up! Mind your own business!

157
00:08:49,080 --> 00:08:49,620
I wonder...

158
00:08:52,440 --> 00:08:53,380
Hey, Ryo-san.

159
00:08:53,780 --> 00:08:55,620
Ryo-san's going wild again, apparently.

160
00:08:55,620 --> 00:08:58,800
His bonus won't get cut, will it?

161
00:08:59,140 --> 00:09:00,700
He still has tabs piling up.

162
00:09:00,700 --> 00:09:03,700
Really. He won't get fired, will he?

163
00:09:03,700 --> 00:09:04,500
Honestly.

164
00:09:04,500 --> 00:09:08,440
Guess I'll go a bit farther.

165
00:09:29,960 --> 00:09:31,960
I ended up all the way in Ueno.

166
00:09:32,880 --> 00:09:34,200
Man, this brings back memories.

167
00:09:34,200 --> 00:09:37,000
I used to play around
here all the time as a kid.

168
00:09:37,480 --> 00:09:39,540
The Ueno woods where I caught
cicadas and dragonflies,

169
00:09:39,540 --> 00:09:42,340
and Shinobazu Pond where I
caught crucian carp and crayfish.

170
00:09:42,720 --> 00:09:43,900
And when I look up,

171
00:09:43,900 --> 00:09:46,100
there's Benten-dō, my favorite...

172
00:09:46,940 --> 00:09:47,300
What?

173
00:09:53,780 --> 00:09:55,300
What's with this "poyoyon" nonsense?

174
00:09:55,300 --> 00:09:58,060
I was just getting
nostalgic about my childhood!

175
00:09:58,060 --> 00:10:00,220
Putting something like this
up in a place like this!

176
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:01,740
Hey, you piece of shit.

177
00:10:02,340 --> 00:10:02,980
Take this, then!

178
00:10:02,980 --> 00:10:03,800
Eat this!

179
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:15,020
No way.

180
00:10:21,540 --> 00:10:24,660
I thought that idiot Ryotsu had
gone and blown up the hotel too,

181
00:10:24,660 --> 00:10:26,680
but it was actually blown up

182
00:10:26,680 --> 00:10:29,440
It's not a blast. It's a "leaf" demolition.

183
00:10:29,440 --> 00:10:30,820
Leaf demolition.

184
00:10:31,320 --> 00:10:36,120
All the pillars were collapsed inward, without
a single piece of debris scattering outside.

185
00:10:36,660 --> 00:10:37,060
I see.

186
00:10:37,460 --> 00:10:40,760
Only a few kilos of
plastic explosive were used.

187
00:10:41,900 --> 00:10:46,700
To bring down a building with that little,
the technique could be called artistic.

188
00:10:47,860 --> 00:10:52,740
But Chief, if Ryotsu didn't do it, isn't
this Katsushika Station's jurisdiction?

189
00:10:53,460 --> 00:10:59,540
Actually, a message announcing the crime
was sent to Katsushika Station's website.

190
00:10:59,540 --> 00:11:00,600
What?!

191
00:11:01,600 --> 00:11:03,940
Chief, when did you start using a computer?

192
00:11:06,180 --> 00:11:11,180
If we can't even use a computer, we can't
deal with high-tech crime from now on.

193
00:11:11,180 --> 00:11:12,660
As expected of the Chief.

194
00:11:14,940 --> 00:11:17,460
Hey, somebody turn on the computer.

195
00:11:23,000 --> 00:11:27,600
At noon tomorrow, I will destroy
the Hotel Sinatra at Shinobazu Pond.

196
00:11:28,300 --> 00:11:29,360
Benten Kozō.

197
00:11:29,900 --> 00:11:34,040
His identity is unknown,
but he is likely to commit further crimes.

198
00:11:34,040 --> 00:11:38,000
Headquarters has also issued
an order to tighten security.

199
00:11:38,000 --> 00:11:43,280
But if the opponent is a bomb professional,
there's nothing we can do.

200
00:11:43,280 --> 00:11:45,160
You can go now.

201
00:11:45,160 --> 00:11:45,580
Yes, sir!

202
00:11:47,840 --> 00:11:54,300
Fortunately, at headquarters' invitation, an
explosives disposal expert has come over from the FBI.

203
00:11:54,300 --> 00:11:55,220
FBI

204
00:11:56,460 --> 00:11:57,180
Please, come in.

205
00:12:04,340 --> 00:12:07,240
I'm Risa Hoshino, from the FBI.

206
00:12:08,120 --> 00:12:10,300
Welcome, Agent Hoshino.

207
00:12:10,300 --> 00:12:13,160
It's an honor to be invited.

208
00:12:13,820 --> 00:12:16,100
The pleasure is ours. Thank you for coming.

209
00:12:17,440 --> 00:12:18,160
Thank you.

210
00:12:19,780 --> 00:12:23,300
When it comes to hating crime,
America and Japan are no different.

211
00:12:24,180 --> 00:12:28,440
I'll do my best to protect this city with all of you.
Nice to meet you.

212
00:12:29,824 --> 00:12:30,936
What fine words.

213
00:12:30,986 --> 00:12:34,140
I wish some idiot had heard that.

214
00:12:34,280 --> 00:12:35,520
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

215
00:12:36,140 --> 00:12:38,203
FBI? How pompous.

216
00:12:38,253 --> 00:12:42,480
So what if she is? Big deal.

217
00:12:43,640 --> 00:12:46,788
Risa-san, you know, is a brilliant
woman who graduated from Yale,

218
00:12:46,838 --> 00:12:49,700
and she's a top elite in
the bomb disposal squad.

219
00:12:49,940 --> 00:12:53,075
Elite or hard candy, I don't know,

220
00:12:53,125 --> 00:12:56,160
but it's none of my business. Anyway.

221
00:12:56,160 --> 00:12:58,640
Wow! Ryo-san's amazing!

222
00:12:59,340 --> 00:13:02,060
Heh heh, how about this?
I've got more of these!

223
00:13:04,460 --> 00:13:08,320
Honestly, you're only good at playing around,
and that's no use to anyone.

224
00:13:09,640 --> 00:13:13,220
But this is communication with the local residents,
isn't it?

225
00:13:13,220 --> 00:13:14,197
Anyway,

226
00:13:14,247 --> 00:13:17,740
you're joining the explosives
disposal seminar too.

227
00:13:17,740 --> 00:13:20,680
Whoa! I'm already fed up with bombs!

228
00:13:20,680 --> 00:13:22,620
Just take part, no arguments.

229
00:13:23,920 --> 00:13:28,820
Explosives are broadly divided into
low explosives and high explosives,

230
00:13:29,220 --> 00:13:31,940
the former mainly being
primers and propellants.

231
00:13:31,940 --> 00:13:34,320
The latter are used for destruction.

232
00:13:34,940 --> 00:13:39,000
Explosions are triggered by the detonator,
so remove it.

233
00:13:39,380 --> 00:13:43,660
Alternatively, you can neutralize it by
cutting the wire connecting the detonator.

234
00:13:44,840 --> 00:13:49,480
For explosives that cannot be removed,
flash-cool them with liquid nitrogen,

235
00:13:49,820 --> 00:13:51,740
and there's also a way to strip
away their explosive function.

236
00:13:53,440 --> 00:13:55,580
Now, let's move on to the
practical disposal training.

237
00:13:58,760 --> 00:14:00,220
Dandy, come on!

238
00:14:09,140 --> 00:14:09,860
What is this?

239
00:14:14,080 --> 00:14:15,160
It's a robot, isn't it?

240
00:14:16,040 --> 00:14:18,680
Co-developed with NASA's
Mars exploration team,

241
00:14:18,680 --> 00:14:21,960
this high-performance explosive
ordnance disposal robot is Dandy.

242
00:14:23,100 --> 00:14:25,000
Dandy, are you ready?

243
00:14:25,580 --> 00:14:27,580
Please enter a command.

244
00:14:28,040 --> 00:14:30,660
It's a robot,
yet it can even speak human language.

245
00:14:31,260 --> 00:14:33,860
It has artificial intelligence, you know.

246
00:14:33,860 --> 00:14:37,340
It's about a hundred times
smarter than certain someone I know.

247
00:14:44,980 --> 00:14:45,960
Dandy.

248
00:14:47,740 --> 00:14:49,880
Roger. Executing command.

249
00:15:09,980 --> 00:15:13,400
I dismantled the chair of the idiot writing this,
you know.

250
00:15:14,320 --> 00:15:14,960
I wonder...

251
00:15:18,340 --> 00:15:24,780
Ow ow ow ow ow! It's made of
hyper titanium on the fixing side.

252
00:15:25,560 --> 00:15:32,380
Hyper titanium. So it's on a completely different
level from any bomb disposal machine so far

253
00:15:32,800 --> 00:15:34,400
Don't get cocky just because you're hard!

254
00:15:34,960 --> 00:15:35,620
No.

255
00:15:35,620 --> 00:15:37,660
In every single ability.

256
00:15:37,660 --> 00:15:40,180
Dandy is the best robot in the world.

257
00:15:40,180 --> 00:15:41,080
What did you say?

258
00:15:41,080 --> 00:15:42,880
Alright, just wait a minute.

259
00:15:45,000 --> 00:15:46,400
I wonder what they're planning to do.

260
00:15:46,400 --> 00:15:48,560
It's bound to be nothing good.

261
00:15:51,260 --> 00:15:51,660
Alright.

262
00:15:51,660 --> 00:15:54,160
Alright, look!

263
00:15:55,540 --> 00:15:56,320
This is it!

264
00:15:56,320 --> 00:15:58,680
The masterpiece of all
the robots I've built!

265
00:15:58,680 --> 00:16:00,680
It's Densuke 28!

266
00:16:02,380 --> 00:16:04,340
When did you make something like that...?

267
00:16:04,340 --> 00:16:08,673
To win the 3 million yen prize at
the upcoming robot sumo tournament,

268
00:16:08,723 --> 00:16:11,880
I spent my summer vacation finishing it!

269
00:16:12,780 --> 00:16:15,798
If you're so sure that
your robot is superior,

270
00:16:15,848 --> 00:16:18,220
go up against this Densuke 28!

271
00:16:19,880 --> 00:16:22,100
Fine, I accept the challenge.

272
00:16:38,340 --> 00:16:38,735
Now then,

273
00:16:38,785 --> 00:16:44,580
you two will each use your robots
to defuse the bomb's timer device.

274
00:16:44,580 --> 00:16:48,840
Starting at the sound of the gong,
whoever finishes first wins, of course.

275
00:16:48,840 --> 00:16:52,200
The moment one of you loses,
the iron ball above the loser will drop.

276
00:16:52,200 --> 00:16:54,620
Win and you're in heaven,
lose and you're in hell.

277
00:16:54,620 --> 00:16:57,120
Are you both ready?

278
00:17:00,900 --> 00:17:03,020
Then, ready, go!

279
00:17:03,540 --> 00:17:05,460
Dandy, roger.

280
00:17:06,440 --> 00:17:07,720
Don't lose, Densuke!

281
00:17:19,160 --> 00:17:22,840
Aaaah! Why aren't you doing anything?

282
00:17:23,460 --> 00:17:29,240
Dandy is a robot with AI. Once you give it a command,
it judges and acts on its own.

283
00:17:30,540 --> 00:17:31,880
At this rate, we're going to lose.

284
00:17:38,120 --> 00:17:46,360
Serves you right! When it's about to lose, it interferes with the opponent.
It's just like its creator, a robot exactly like the man who built it.

285
00:17:52,500 --> 00:17:53,740
You son of a bitch!

286
00:17:54,280 --> 00:17:58,100
Dandy is programmed to protect
itself from external threats.

287
00:17:58,100 --> 00:18:01,000
Now it's time for our secret weapon.

288
00:18:13,480 --> 00:18:16,000
Continue dismantling Dandy.

289
00:18:16,000 --> 00:18:16,740
Understood.

290
00:18:25,740 --> 00:18:26,820
Yes.

291
00:18:26,820 --> 00:18:27,600
Yes, the red one.

292
00:18:27,600 --> 00:18:30,960
Okay!

293
00:18:31,010 --> 00:18:34,420
That's it!

294
00:18:40,400 --> 00:18:46,080
My Densuke 28 hasn't even entered
the robot sumo tournament yet!

295
00:18:46,080 --> 00:18:49,620
Looks like the match is decided,
Officer Ryotsu.

296
00:18:54,780 --> 00:18:59,320
Already forgotten? Repeating the same mistake.
You really are a monkey-brain.

297
00:19:00,020 --> 00:19:00,660
What did you say?

298
00:19:00,660 --> 00:19:02,540
Warning! Warning!

299
00:19:02,540 --> 00:19:04,000
Shut up! What's with the warning?

300
00:19:04,420 --> 00:19:06,320
Be careful, Officer Ryotsu.

301
00:19:11,440 --> 00:19:14,040
Enemy intel: it's some skunk-like thing.

302
00:19:14,040 --> 00:19:16,680
That's why I told you to be careful.

303
00:19:16,680 --> 00:19:22,100
Incoming call from Metropolitan Police HQ. An incident has occurred.
Please gather at the investigation headquarters immediately.

304
00:19:23,020 --> 00:19:23,920
Hey, what?

305
00:19:26,680 --> 00:19:27,940
Did something happen?

306
00:19:28,580 --> 00:19:31,820
Benten Kozo has sent another
message announcing a new crime.

307
00:19:31,820 --> 00:19:32,900
What?!

308
00:19:42,220 --> 00:19:43,560
Tomorrow at midnight.

309
00:19:44,160 --> 00:19:46,520
They're going to destroy the
Sinatra Moonlight Building.

310
00:19:47,280 --> 00:19:48,340
Benten Kozō.

311
00:19:48,900 --> 00:19:50,420
Sinatra's building again?

312
00:19:51,440 --> 00:19:53,940
Maybe the culprit is after Sinatra.

313
00:19:54,600 --> 00:19:57,080
Who exactly is this Sinatra?

314
00:19:58,500 --> 00:20:01,040
His real name is Shinada Torazō, age 56.

315
00:20:01,620 --> 00:20:03,860
President of Sinatra Trading Co., Ltd.

316
00:20:04,420 --> 00:20:07,860
Hotels, cabaret management, trading,
resort development, and more.

317
00:20:07,860 --> 00:20:09,620
He runs a wide range of businesses,

318
00:20:10,160 --> 00:20:14,040
but he's been arrested on suspicion of fraud, embezzlement,
forging private documents, breach of trust, and so on.

319
00:20:14,040 --> 00:20:16,260
He's been arrested 36 times.

320
00:20:16,260 --> 00:20:18,920
But every case was
dropped without prosecution.

321
00:20:19,500 --> 00:20:20,600
All of them without prosecution?

322
00:20:21,580 --> 00:20:24,680
Martin,
Sinatra's secretary and legal adviser.

323
00:20:24,680 --> 00:20:28,620
Apparently this guy wins in
court through sheer trickery.

324
00:20:29,520 --> 00:20:31,820
Well, he's a man with a terrible reputation.

325
00:20:31,820 --> 00:20:33,138
Even if he's a bad man,

326
00:20:33,188 --> 00:20:36,440
my job is to stop the bombing.

327
00:20:53,880 --> 00:20:56,640
Why do I have to be the partner?!

328
00:20:56,940 --> 00:20:58,580
Because it's a dangerous mission!

329
00:20:58,680 --> 00:21:01,140
You're the only one who
wouldn't mind if he died!

330
00:21:01,820 --> 00:21:03,600
That's cruel, Chief!

331
00:21:09,600 --> 00:21:13,040
Am I a prize from a UFO catcher?! Idiot!

332
00:21:24,740 --> 00:21:28,140
President, there's a call for you from
Chief Ohara of the Katsushika station.

333
00:21:28,660 --> 00:21:29,400
Put him on.

334
00:21:29,600 --> 00:21:30,000
Yes.

335
00:21:33,660 --> 00:21:34,520
Speaking.

336
00:21:36,160 --> 00:21:36,500
What?

337
00:21:38,660 --> 00:21:43,100
We've received a threat from Benten Kozō
that he'll destroy Moonlight Building.

338
00:21:43,100 --> 00:21:46,820
An explosives expert is on
their way to defuse it now.

339
00:21:49,840 --> 00:21:50,520
Right now.

340
00:21:51,240 --> 00:21:52,180
Help me.

341
00:22:03,120 --> 00:22:19,660
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah!

342
00:22:20,440 --> 00:22:23,500
Now that we're a team,
make sure you don't become a burden

343
00:22:25,220 --> 00:22:25,860
got it?!

344
00:22:33,380 --> 00:22:35,900
What, a blackout? It's pitch-black in here!

345
00:22:36,740 --> 00:22:38,930
The culprit must have cut
the power to get in our way,

346
00:22:38,980 --> 00:22:40,940
so they must have tampered
with the electrical system.

347
00:22:41,980 --> 00:22:42,300
What's that?

348
00:22:43,740 --> 00:22:46,100
Infrared-illuminating night-vision goggles.

349
00:22:47,160 --> 00:22:49,680
Well, if you had those,
why didn't you say so sooner?

350
00:22:50,920 --> 00:22:52,360
I can see! I can see!

351
00:22:52,740 --> 00:22:56,260
They also have thermal
detection and laser rangefinding.

352
00:22:58,040 --> 00:22:59,240
This is handy.

353
00:23:00,940 --> 00:23:04,580
What's that? The color of part
of the pillar is slightly off.

354
00:23:05,120 --> 00:23:08,200
It's camouflaged,
but that's where explosives were planted.

355
00:23:08,200 --> 00:23:09,900
So there's a bomb there?

356
00:23:10,740 --> 00:23:12,460
But over there too.

357
00:23:12,460 --> 00:23:13,700
Oh?

358
00:23:14,560 --> 00:23:15,240
Here too.

359
00:23:16,100 --> 00:23:16,820
There as well.

360
00:23:17,260 --> 00:23:18,600
W-why so many?

361
00:23:19,340 --> 00:23:22,860
The culprit is applying the technique
of controlled building demolition.

362
00:23:23,220 --> 00:23:23,540
What?

363
00:23:24,660 --> 00:23:27,580
Multiple explosives placed
through precise calculations

364
00:23:27,920 --> 00:23:30,440
are set to detonate with
exact time intervals,

365
00:23:30,780 --> 00:23:35,100
and with only a tiny amount of explosive,
the building collapses under its own weight.

366
00:23:35,900 --> 00:23:38,120
without damaging the surrounding buildings.

367
00:23:38,960 --> 00:23:43,280
What we need to find is the detonator
controlling all of those explosives.

368
00:23:43,960 --> 00:23:44,280
I see.

369
00:23:46,100 --> 00:23:47,060
Let's split up and search.

370
00:23:47,060 --> 00:23:48,440
Dandy!

371
00:23:49,600 --> 00:23:51,740
Hey, weren't we supposed to be a team?

372
00:24:08,060 --> 00:24:09,200
This is President Shinada.

373
00:24:09,200 --> 00:24:11,900
Why does it always have to
be our building they target?

374
00:24:11,900 --> 00:24:14,580
We'd have to ask Benten Kozō about that.

375
00:24:16,580 --> 00:24:17,520
Who is he?

376
00:24:17,520 --> 00:24:19,840
We're still investigating that as well.

377
00:24:20,660 --> 00:24:25,200
People like those useless fools are what
you call a waste of taxpayers' money.

378
00:24:25,200 --> 00:24:29,220
Look who's talking,
when you don't even pay your taxes properly.

379
00:24:29,960 --> 00:24:31,620
There are rumors he's been evading taxes.

380
00:24:31,620 --> 00:24:34,140
Apparently he's hiding a huge
amount of money somewhere.

381
00:24:37,460 --> 00:24:39,760
Treating me like a damn nuisance

382
00:24:39,760 --> 00:24:43,340
Found it! Come here, Officer Ryotsu.

383
00:24:47,180 --> 00:24:48,100
Did you find it?

384
00:24:49,420 --> 00:24:51,520
If you're turning on the light,
say so first!

385
00:24:52,960 --> 00:24:53,620
Here it is.

386
00:24:56,340 --> 00:24:57,320
Right here, of all places.

387
00:24:58,300 --> 00:25:00,640
Because the wiring has to
run through the whole building.

388
00:25:00,640 --> 00:25:02,860
I thought the air vents
would be easy to use.

389
00:25:03,440 --> 00:25:04,080
Dandy!

390
00:25:05,700 --> 00:25:07,300
Damn it, you did it now!

391
00:25:07,300 --> 00:25:08,220
Krrsh!

392
00:25:09,920 --> 00:25:11,520
I cut it again.

393
00:25:14,980 --> 00:25:15,660
What's wrong?

394
00:25:19,780 --> 00:25:22,120
Uh-oh, looks like the
drive system broke down.

395
00:25:22,960 --> 00:25:25,240
Wasn't it supposed to be hyper-titanium?

396
00:25:25,680 --> 00:25:27,660
If the arms and legs don't extend,
we can't carry out the disposal.

397
00:25:27,660 --> 00:25:28,980
Got it, got it.

398
00:25:28,980 --> 00:25:31,200
I'll just lift Dandy up, then, right?

399
00:25:31,740 --> 00:25:33,640
That's impossible. How many kilos is it?

400
00:25:37,800 --> 00:25:38,440
Well?

401
00:25:39,520 --> 00:25:39,840
No way.

402
00:25:41,280 --> 00:25:42,620
It's 350 kilos!

403
00:25:42,620 --> 00:25:42,880
What?

404
00:25:44,340 --> 00:25:46,860
3...350 kilos...

405
00:25:46,860 --> 00:25:49,120
Ugh, just hurry up.

406
00:25:54,880 --> 00:25:58,320
Boss, if by any chance someone finds that...

407
00:25:58,840 --> 00:26:02,280
Don't worry. Those guys won't find it.

408
00:26:11,420 --> 00:26:12,440
Are you done yet!

409
00:26:23,720 --> 00:26:24,440
What's wrong?

410
00:26:24,980 --> 00:26:28,120
The dimensional device short-circuited
and the countdown sped up!

411
00:26:28,540 --> 00:26:29,160
What the hell?

412
00:26:29,840 --> 00:26:32,720
Thirty seconds left,
there's no time to disarm it now!

413
00:26:33,140 --> 00:26:36,460
What are you talking about?
You're the FBI, aren't you? Do something!

414
00:26:36,460 --> 00:26:39,380
I want to do something,
but you're the one who smashed it up!

415
00:26:39,380 --> 00:26:42,040
I'm lifting this damn heavy thing here!

416
00:26:42,660 --> 00:26:43,820
Twenty seconds left!

417
00:26:44,340 --> 00:26:46,520
Wouldn't it be better to
run away than to squabble?

418
00:26:46,660 --> 00:26:48,320
Twenty seconds! Run!

419
00:26:52,500 --> 00:26:54,640
Are they going to be all right?
The senior officers?

420
00:26:54,640 --> 00:26:56,900
They'll manage somehow, won't they?

421
00:26:56,900 --> 00:26:58,320
What's with the FBI?

422
00:26:58,320 --> 00:27:00,640
Everyone, get away!

423
00:27:01,280 --> 00:27:01,780
What?

424
00:27:02,660 --> 00:27:03,980
It's going to explode!

425
00:27:33,320 --> 00:27:39,440
My castle of honor and glory,
the Moonlight Building...

426
00:27:45,580 --> 00:27:46,020
What?

427
00:27:47,620 --> 00:27:48,520
Martin!

428
00:27:48,520 --> 00:27:49,380
Yes.

429
00:27:49,380 --> 00:27:50,560
Dandy!

430
00:27:53,980 --> 00:27:58,540
Hey, hey, this, no, this,
stop it, stop it, this!

431
00:27:58,540 --> 00:28:00,060
What are you doing?

432
00:28:00,060 --> 00:28:09,840
!

433
00:28:10,700 --> 00:28:13,100
Hey, it's a stack of bills!
A stack of bills!

434
00:28:13,100 --> 00:28:16,360
Idiot! That money is
evidence of tax evasion.

435
00:28:16,360 --> 00:28:17,200
Tax evasion?

436
00:28:20,240 --> 00:28:23,820
President Shinada,
please come with us to the station.

437
00:28:26,800 --> 00:28:28,700
President, come with us.

438
00:28:35,080 --> 00:28:39,040
So you're saying the building
collapsed because of me?

439
00:28:39,840 --> 00:28:42,502
That's right.
If you hadn't roughed up Dandy,

440
00:28:42,552 --> 00:28:44,180
it wouldn't have malfunctioned.

441
00:28:44,680 --> 00:28:46,820
He started it first!

442
00:28:47,080 --> 00:28:49,840
Ryotsu, you're not going
to blame the robot, are you?

443
00:28:50,100 --> 00:28:50,500
Chief!

444
00:28:51,140 --> 00:28:53,581
But thanks to Sinatra's
building falling apart,

445
00:28:53,631 --> 00:28:56,400
we found evidence of Sinatra's tax evasion.

446
00:28:56,740 --> 00:28:57,557
Exactly.

447
00:28:57,607 --> 00:29:01,077
Sinatra got released on
100 million yen bail, though,

448
00:29:01,127 --> 00:29:03,760
but that's still a win for Ryo-chan,
isn't it?

449
00:29:04,520 --> 00:29:06,520
That's one thing, and this is another.

450
00:29:19,900 --> 00:29:21,120
Damn it!

451
00:29:21,120 --> 00:29:23,740
This is your fault, you damn machine!

452
00:29:23,740 --> 00:29:25,740
I'll teach you a lesson!

453
00:29:25,740 --> 00:29:27,740
Warning, warning!

454
00:29:27,740 --> 00:29:29,060
Shut up already!

455
00:29:47,080 --> 00:29:48,500
I like it too.

456
00:29:49,380 --> 00:29:52,320
Watching people go about
their lives like this,

457
00:29:53,880 --> 00:29:54,320
yeah.

458
00:29:55,180 --> 00:29:57,220
I love this town.

459
00:29:57,220 --> 00:30:01,060
That's why I'm glad I get
to be a police officer here.

460
00:30:01,060 --> 00:30:03,960
Risa, why did you choose your current job?

461
00:30:05,700 --> 00:30:07,240
Why would you ask that?

462
00:30:07,240 --> 00:30:09,540
Well, it's a dangerous job, after all.

463
00:30:11,260 --> 00:30:11,780
Aren't your family worried about you?

464
00:30:12,820 --> 00:30:14,080
I don't have any family.

465
00:30:15,140 --> 00:30:16,340
I'm sorry.

466
00:30:16,940 --> 00:30:17,700
It's fine.

467
00:30:20,340 --> 00:30:21,900
Something's wrong with Dandy.

468
00:30:23,960 --> 00:30:25,960
Risa-san, the alarm is going off now.

469
00:30:25,960 --> 00:30:26,240
Yes.

470
00:30:26,800 --> 00:30:31,560
That's the Chief!

471
00:30:32,440 --> 00:30:35,700
What are you doing in a place like this?

472
00:30:36,200 --> 00:30:39,740
Well, someone scribbled graffiti on Dandy.

473
00:30:41,260 --> 00:30:51,380
What do you mean? What's with that graffiti? You didn't do it yourself, did you?
Don't joke around, we're good friends, so... Dandy-chan~

474
00:30:51,380 --> 00:30:52,560
Junsa-chan~

475
00:30:54,560 --> 00:30:59,480
Chief Ohara, there might be
something on this security camera.

476
00:31:06,060 --> 00:31:09,420
That's right.
The culprit might be on this footage too.

477
00:31:09,960 --> 00:31:13,440
But running security cameras
inside a police station?

478
00:31:13,980 --> 00:31:17,280
That just shows how
important Dandy is as a robot.

479
00:31:18,500 --> 00:31:21,380
This is your fault, you machine!

480
00:31:22,220 --> 00:31:24,020
Doesn't it sound like your voice?

481
00:31:24,020 --> 00:31:25,880
No, it isn't.

482
00:31:26,940 --> 00:31:29,600
Chief, the culprit is wearing
a police officer's uniform.

483
00:31:30,920 --> 00:31:32,560
I'll deal with you like this!

484
00:31:32,560 --> 00:31:36,940
Sneaking into the vehicle in a fake uniform...
that's quite a clever criminal.

485
00:31:36,940 --> 00:31:38,500
Warning! Warning!

486
00:31:38,500 --> 00:31:42,600
Shut up, you dimwit!
Don't underestimate the Japanese police!

487
00:31:42,600 --> 00:31:46,260
I'm amazed. I never imagined
he'd disguise himself as me.

488
00:31:46,260 --> 00:31:49,620
Could he be some spy from a
foreign country or something?

489
00:31:49,620 --> 00:31:52,540
No matter how you look at it,
he's exactly you.

490
00:31:52,540 --> 00:31:56,500
That can't be right.
Let's look further ahead.

491
00:31:56,500 --> 00:31:59,180
After this,
he's surely going to get beaten up by Basco.

492
00:32:00,820 --> 00:32:03,020
You're suspended for two weeks.

493
00:32:03,020 --> 00:32:05,700
Starting tomorrow,
you don't have to come to the police box.

494
00:32:05,700 --> 00:32:09,300
So that means I get paid
without having to work?

495
00:32:09,300 --> 00:32:10,400
You idiot!

496
00:32:10,400 --> 00:32:12,700
During your suspension,
don't set foot outside the dorm.

497
00:32:12,700 --> 00:32:15,200
You won't get paid for that time.

498
00:32:55,220 --> 00:32:56,500
Hey, Nakagawa.

499
00:32:57,140 --> 00:32:58,380
"Hey" yourself!

500
00:32:58,380 --> 00:32:59,400
Sakonji-san!

501
00:32:59,400 --> 00:33:00,600
Watch it!

502
00:33:01,000 --> 00:33:03,060
You almost got shot!

503
00:33:03,420 --> 00:33:04,300
Volvo-san!

504
00:33:04,300 --> 00:33:05,760
What are you doing?

505
00:33:06,380 --> 00:33:10,500
No hard feelings, but we've been
ordered not to let Ryotsu out.

506
00:33:10,980 --> 00:33:15,440
Then shouldn't you be watching the senior officer
inside rather than the people coming from outside?

507
00:33:15,440 --> 00:33:17,140
Right.

508
00:33:20,140 --> 00:33:21,160
Excuse me.

509
00:33:22,960 --> 00:33:25,420
Senpai, I came to check on you.

510
00:33:26,980 --> 00:33:27,600
Senpai?

511
00:33:30,280 --> 00:33:31,160
Are you sleeping?

512
00:33:32,000 --> 00:33:32,720
Whoa!

513
00:33:35,360 --> 00:33:36,560
A decoy?

514
00:33:38,820 --> 00:33:40,040
Heave!

515
00:33:40,040 --> 00:33:40,920
Senpai.

516
00:33:40,920 --> 00:33:43,020
Nagano. What's up?

517
00:33:43,260 --> 00:33:45,260
Don't "what's up" me.

518
00:33:45,680 --> 00:33:47,560
I figured you'd be bored,
being on suspension.

519
00:33:47,560 --> 00:33:49,460
So I brought you some treats.

520
00:33:49,940 --> 00:33:52,460
Isn't that Iseya's dorayaki, your favorite?

521
00:33:52,460 --> 00:33:53,540
You're thoughtful.

522
00:33:53,540 --> 00:33:55,280
What are you doing?

523
00:33:55,660 --> 00:33:58,240
And if Volvo-san or Sakonji finds out...

524
00:33:58,240 --> 00:34:01,700
Those two have nothing
but muscle for brains.

525
00:34:04,120 --> 00:34:07,440
You see, I was reading this manga,
and it said that around here,

526
00:34:08,200 --> 00:34:13,060
look, look! There was an article saying the Tokugawa
shogunate's buried gold is buried right here.

527
00:34:14,240 --> 00:34:17,400
Isn't this the 1968 issue
of Weekly Shonen Jump?

528
00:34:17,400 --> 00:34:20,280
I haven't heard that it's been found yet.

529
00:34:20,700 --> 00:34:24,120
Each piece is worth at least 5 million yen,
you know.

530
00:34:24,120 --> 00:34:27,500
If we find them all,
it's a treasure worth billions of yen!

531
00:34:28,020 --> 00:34:31,940
But around here, my father's
company is building a subway line.

532
00:34:32,960 --> 00:34:35,840
So Nakagawa Consulun has
its eye on the treasure too?

533
00:34:37,020 --> 00:34:38,060
This one's mine!

534
00:34:38,060 --> 00:34:40,060
That's not it, senpai.

535
00:34:42,380 --> 00:34:46,040
No way we're letting the
Nakagawa Group get there first!

536
00:34:49,740 --> 00:34:52,240
The treasure detector's already starting up!

537
00:34:53,220 --> 00:34:54,360
Okay, this way!

538
00:35:08,380 --> 00:35:09,360
Yay!

539
00:35:09,880 --> 00:35:11,160
Come on, come on!

540
00:35:11,660 --> 00:35:12,540
Best up!

541
00:35:13,800 --> 00:35:16,080
Boss, what's wrong?

542
00:35:16,080 --> 00:35:17,160
Yay!

543
00:35:17,600 --> 00:35:18,960
What's this side tunnel?

544
00:35:18,960 --> 00:35:21,100
I didn't hear anything about this.

545
00:35:21,100 --> 00:35:24,360
Maybe another team dug it?

546
00:35:26,060 --> 00:35:29,020
There must have been a
change in the route plan.

547
00:35:29,020 --> 00:35:29,960
Yay!

548
00:35:30,300 --> 00:35:31,460
Follow me!

549
00:35:33,720 --> 00:35:34,760
Full speed ahead!

550
00:35:36,040 --> 00:35:36,680
Yes, sir!

551
00:35:37,520 --> 00:35:38,080
Can't wait!

552
00:35:38,320 --> 00:35:49,020
Chief.

553
00:35:49,020 --> 00:35:50,363
Nakagawa. How's it going?

554
00:35:50,413 --> 00:35:53,200
Has Ryotsu been behaving
himself during his suspension?

555
00:35:53,320 --> 00:35:54,831
Y-yes, of course,

556
00:35:54,881 --> 00:35:57,863
with Sakonji and Volvo-san keeping watch,

557
00:35:57,913 --> 00:35:59,780
he can't set foot outside.

558
00:35:59,780 --> 00:36:01,557
Good, that's a relief.

559
00:36:01,607 --> 00:36:04,500
With Ryotsu out of the picture,
we can relax for a while.

560
00:36:04,700 --> 00:36:06,560
Chief, your tea is ready.

561
00:36:07,040 --> 00:36:08,180
Thanks.

562
00:36:11,000 --> 00:36:11,660
Reiko.

563
00:36:12,960 --> 00:36:15,720
Actually, senior,
we're digging for buried treasure.

564
00:36:15,940 --> 00:36:16,840
Buried treasure?

565
00:36:17,320 --> 00:36:19,580
An earthquake?

566
00:36:28,560 --> 00:36:30,700
Hey, the wire's swaying has changed!

567
00:36:31,260 --> 00:36:32,440
Alright, this way!

568
00:36:40,420 --> 00:36:43,680
Garuto-kun, the direction changed again!

569
00:36:44,180 --> 00:36:45,680
It's moving really fast!

570
00:36:45,680 --> 00:36:48,660
Yes! Anyway, follow me!

571
00:36:57,720 --> 00:36:59,140
What on earth is that?

572
00:36:59,140 --> 00:37:00,660
Isn't it a mole?

573
00:37:00,660 --> 00:37:03,880
There's no way a mole that huge exists!

574
00:37:04,400 --> 00:37:06,720
Only one person could have come
up with something like that.

575
00:37:07,380 --> 00:37:08,440
Ryo-chan

576
00:37:45,960 --> 00:37:49,200
I never imagined garbage
could be such a good business.

577
00:37:59,080 --> 00:38:02,580
Chief! There's a Benten Kozo
crime warning on the internet!

578
00:38:03,480 --> 00:38:04,200
What!?

579
00:38:12,620 --> 00:38:13,765
At noon today,

580
00:38:13,815 --> 00:38:17,640
he'll destroy the Sinatra Ocean Building.

581
00:38:18,420 --> 00:38:19,280
Benten Kozo.

582
00:38:20,120 --> 00:38:21,760
The Sinatra building again?

583
00:38:23,140 --> 00:38:26,500
That Benten Kozo!
We don't have much time, hurry!

584
00:38:31,580 --> 00:38:32,960
Found Kenta.

585
00:38:35,200 --> 00:38:36,960
Alright, now just Asuka left.

586
00:38:37,960 --> 00:38:39,880
A patrol car! Let's go check it out.

587
00:38:53,400 --> 00:38:55,480
So that's the Sinatra Ocean Building.

588
00:39:01,260 --> 00:39:04,220
Didn't this used to be
a playground for children?

589
00:39:05,200 --> 00:39:06,700
And in the meantime,
they built that weird building...

590
00:39:15,940 --> 00:39:18,900
Hey, are you saying our
building is being targeted again?

591
00:39:18,900 --> 00:39:23,720
President,
what on earth was this building built for?

592
00:39:24,620 --> 00:39:25,900
It's a trade secret.

593
00:39:27,020 --> 00:39:29,520
Isn't he hiding something again?

594
00:39:30,300 --> 00:39:31,700
Hey, that's rude.

595
00:39:32,200 --> 00:39:35,980
Instead of that, why don't you
hurry up and arrest Benten Kozo?

596
00:39:37,940 --> 00:39:39,320
I have no words to answer that.

597
00:39:44,560 --> 00:39:54,240
Dandy, hurry!

598
00:39:54,240 --> 00:39:55,320
Roger!

599
00:39:55,920 --> 00:39:56,980
Lisa-san!

600
00:39:58,960 --> 00:39:59,980
We don't have time.

601
00:40:02,540 --> 00:40:06,580
Wait! If you fail this time,
how do you plan to take responsibility?

602
00:40:07,280 --> 00:40:07,880
Responsibility?

603
00:40:07,880 --> 00:40:11,760
Of course!
You'll take responsibility for any failure!

604
00:40:12,320 --> 00:40:15,040
Unless we get out,
the minister will never accept it, you know.

605
00:40:16,900 --> 00:40:18,080
Another earthquake!

606
00:40:18,680 --> 00:40:20,380
Move, move, move, move!

607
00:40:20,380 --> 00:40:27,220
The treasure's right nearby!

608
00:40:27,660 --> 00:40:28,300
Yes!

609
00:40:58,800 --> 00:41:01,780
You snuck in here and played without permission,
didn't you?

610
00:41:01,780 --> 00:41:05,020
This used to be our playground, you know!

611
00:41:05,840 --> 00:41:07,640
That's right, give back our playground!

612
00:41:07,640 --> 00:41:11,140
Shut up! Talk back again and I'll smack you!

613
00:41:11,140 --> 00:41:12,980
Cut it out!

614
00:41:15,720 --> 00:41:17,260
We only have seven minutes left.

615
00:41:17,260 --> 00:41:21,280
Damn Benten Kozo,
dragging kids into this too!

616
00:41:22,580 --> 00:41:23,980
I would never do something like that.

617
00:41:26,140 --> 00:41:29,300
No, I will definitely rescue her.

618
00:41:29,700 --> 00:41:30,340
Risa-san.

619
00:41:32,360 --> 00:41:34,760
We haven't given you
permission to enter yet!

620
00:41:39,700 --> 00:41:41,680
Asuka-chan, where are you?

621
00:41:42,780 --> 00:41:45,700
Asuka-chan, come out!
Hide-and-seek is over now.

622
00:41:47,940 --> 00:41:51,660
Asuka-chan, answer me! Asuka-chan!

623
00:41:58,820 --> 00:41:59,620
Asuka-chan!

624
00:41:59,620 --> 00:42:00,220
Asuka-chaaan!

625
00:42:03,020 --> 00:42:06,000
I never thought it would come to this.
What do we do?

626
00:42:19,900 --> 00:42:21,520
Asuka-chan

627
00:42:21,520 --> 00:42:23,920
Asuka-chan

628
00:42:28,980 --> 00:42:31,340
Asuka-chan

629
00:42:31,340 --> 00:42:34,260
Yay!

630
00:42:37,260 --> 00:42:43,320
What the hell is this! Damn it! I thought it was a mountain of treasure,
but it's a mountain of oil drums!

631
00:42:43,700 --> 00:42:45,100
What is this supposed to be!

632
00:42:45,160 --> 00:42:45,660
Asuka-chan, Officer Ryuto is searching

633
00:42:46,920 --> 00:42:47,460
Ebi!

634
00:42:48,520 --> 00:42:48,880
Wait!

635
00:42:49,300 --> 00:42:49,640
What?

636
00:42:50,520 --> 00:42:52,880
Please, lend us a hand!
We're looking for a little girl!

637
00:42:53,080 --> 00:42:53,340
What?

638
00:42:54,560 --> 00:42:58,040
This building is going to be destroyed
by Benten Kozo in five minutes!

639
00:42:58,580 --> 00:42:59,180
What!

640
00:43:03,120 --> 00:43:05,140
What on earth is this building!

641
00:43:06,000 --> 00:43:07,400
An industrial waste processing plant.

642
00:43:08,200 --> 00:43:08,920
What?

643
00:43:09,360 --> 00:43:11,580
Never mind that right now!

644
00:43:14,180 --> 00:43:15,340
It's a detonator.

645
00:43:15,340 --> 00:43:16,960
We only have three minutes left.

646
00:43:17,760 --> 00:43:19,060
Where are you, Asuka-chan?

647
00:43:19,060 --> 00:43:20,220
Asuka-chan...

648
00:43:20,220 --> 00:43:21,360
Calm down, Reiko.

649
00:43:21,360 --> 00:43:22,880
How could I possibly calm down?

650
00:43:25,760 --> 00:43:26,500
Reiko...

651
00:43:26,500 --> 00:43:29,220
You don't understand.

652
00:43:30,440 --> 00:43:32,340
how a little girl all alone must feel.

653
00:43:36,400 --> 00:43:38,460
Help! Somebody help me!

654
00:43:42,300 --> 00:43:43,180
It's over there!

655
00:43:44,940 --> 00:43:46,140
Hey! It's Choko!

656
00:43:48,080 --> 00:43:48,920
Is it deep inside here?

657
00:43:49,380 --> 00:43:50,620
In a narrow place like this?

658
00:43:50,620 --> 00:43:52,460
A small child could fit in there.

659
00:43:52,460 --> 00:43:55,240
They got in, but now they can't get out.

660
00:43:56,120 --> 00:43:57,220
We've come to rescue you!

661
00:44:01,880 --> 00:44:05,780
Azoisu, if it comes to this, we have
no choice but to disarm the detonator.

662
00:44:06,340 --> 00:44:11,280
"Disarm it," you say, but without bringing Dandy,
how are we supposed to disarm it?

663
00:44:11,280 --> 00:44:13,400
I can do it. I can.

664
00:44:14,700 --> 00:44:16,120
Hey, Riza.

665
00:44:27,720 --> 00:44:28,760
Way to go, Reiko!

666
00:44:29,720 --> 00:44:31,340
Just like an FBI agent!

667
00:44:31,340 --> 00:44:34,120
Disarming a bomb with just one finger!

668
00:44:34,580 --> 00:44:34,980
Yeah.

669
00:44:36,080 --> 00:44:37,160
Asuka!

670
00:44:37,580 --> 00:44:39,460
Thank goodness she's safe.

671
00:44:40,900 --> 00:44:42,100
She's all right now.

672
00:44:43,480 --> 00:44:45,540
But how did you get her
out of such a narrow place?

673
00:44:46,060 --> 00:44:49,480
I just removed two or three pipes.

674
00:45:02,700 --> 00:45:03,840
The ceiling's collapsing!

675
00:45:03,840 --> 00:45:04,720
Run!

676
00:45:16,880 --> 00:45:18,420
The building's going to collapse!

677
00:45:19,900 --> 00:45:20,740
Reiko-san!

678
00:45:30,780 --> 00:45:31,560
This way!

679
00:45:33,540 --> 00:45:33,940
Hey!

680
00:45:53,540 --> 00:45:54,680
No way.

681
00:45:54,680 --> 00:45:56,240
Shasha-shasha-sha!

682
00:45:57,360 --> 00:45:59,360
You useless fools!

683
00:46:00,780 --> 00:46:01,920
Let's go rescue them!

684
00:46:01,920 --> 00:46:03,400
Get an excavator over here.

685
00:46:03,400 --> 00:46:03,820
Yes, sir.

686
00:46:06,900 --> 00:46:07,620
Hurry up!

687
00:46:15,600 --> 00:46:17,020
They're not there either.

688
00:46:18,320 --> 00:46:18,880
Chief!

689
00:46:18,880 --> 00:46:20,360
There's a hole in the basement.

690
00:46:21,020 --> 00:46:21,380
What?

691
00:46:23,540 --> 00:46:23,900
This is...

692
00:46:24,900 --> 00:46:26,200
It's a mole hole.

693
00:46:27,220 --> 00:46:29,220
Are you still going on about moles?

694
00:46:31,000 --> 00:46:32,860
Eeeeeeeh!

695
00:46:41,920 --> 00:46:43,920
This is gonna be quite a show, isn't it?

696
00:46:43,920 --> 00:46:46,980
Eeeeeh!

697
00:46:49,260 --> 00:46:51,360
That was close... thank goodness we're safe.

698
00:46:52,520 --> 00:46:53,440
It's all right now.

699
00:46:54,120 --> 00:46:54,860
Haah.

700
00:46:54,860 --> 00:46:58,100
Good, you're a brave kid. Were you scared?

701
00:46:58,100 --> 00:47:01,340
I was scared... really, really scared.

702
00:47:01,340 --> 00:47:03,840
Masashi, dinner's ready!

703
00:47:03,840 --> 00:47:04,880
Coming!

704
00:47:04,880 --> 00:47:07,820
Shoko-chan, come home now.

705
00:47:07,820 --> 00:47:09,840
Okay, Mom.

706
00:47:12,340 --> 00:47:13,100
Everyone.

707
00:47:26,800 --> 00:47:28,640
Help!

708
00:47:28,640 --> 00:47:30,640
Somebody, help me!

709
00:47:30,640 --> 00:47:33,600
Help!

710
00:47:41,240 --> 00:47:41,760
Well...

711
00:47:48,380 --> 00:47:49,180
What's wrong?

712
00:47:49,180 --> 00:47:51,340
It's nothing.

713
00:47:52,060 --> 00:47:54,020
But why would there be a
hole in a place like that?

714
00:47:54,020 --> 00:47:56,640
Well, that's because I
was after the treasure...

715
00:47:56,640 --> 00:47:57,100
Treasure?

716
00:47:57,100 --> 00:47:59,560
Right, I can't just stand around here!

717
00:48:00,560 --> 00:48:01,620
Corporal Ryotsu!

718
00:48:06,660 --> 00:48:07,320
Bye-bye!

719
00:48:08,620 --> 00:48:08,960
Ugh, already!

720
00:48:24,240 --> 00:48:28,500
The Sinatra Ocean Building,
destroyed yesterday by Benten Kozo,

721
00:48:28,500 --> 00:48:32,480
was found to have been processing
industrial waste without a permit,

722
00:48:32,480 --> 00:48:37,360
and residents in the area are
campaigning to drive out Sinatra Shokai.

723
00:48:38,080 --> 00:48:42,020
So Sinatra was trying to make
a fortune off waste disposal

724
00:48:42,480 --> 00:48:45,700
Apparently high levels of
dioxin were detected nearby.

725
00:48:46,400 --> 00:48:49,740
So Benten Kozo exposed Sinatra's wrongdoing again,
is that it?

726
00:48:50,460 --> 00:48:52,440
Well, that's what it comes down to.

727
00:48:52,940 --> 00:48:56,020
If anyone deserves praise,
it's Reiko-san for rescuing that child.

728
00:48:56,880 --> 00:49:00,360
But we still haven't managed to stop the building from being destroyed,
not even once.

729
00:49:00,980 --> 00:49:01,940
Now that you mention it, that's true.

730
00:49:04,140 --> 00:49:06,060
Something about this bugs me a little.

731
00:49:06,060 --> 00:49:22,780
Oops-a-daisy!

732
00:49:25,120 --> 00:49:26,680
Corporal Ryotsu!

733
00:49:26,680 --> 00:49:29,580
We meet again, Reiko.

734
00:49:30,060 --> 00:49:31,120
What are you doing?

735
00:49:32,480 --> 00:49:34,720
Look who's talking.
You're still treasure hunting?

736
00:49:34,920 --> 00:49:37,480
I'm taking a break. I'm starving.

737
00:49:42,160 --> 00:49:46,000
That's the Odaiba side, isn't it?
Are they filming something at Fuji TV again?

738
00:49:46,460 --> 00:49:47,000
Yeah.

739
00:49:47,300 --> 00:49:49,900
How about a dorayaki from Iseya?

740
00:49:50,100 --> 00:49:51,360
Thanks.

741
00:49:55,500 --> 00:49:59,300
Speaking of which, when I was a kid,
I used to eat bread around here

742
00:49:59,300 --> 00:50:02,020
and watch that Katsutoki Bridge open.

743
00:50:02,020 --> 00:50:03,720
The Katsutoki Bridge opens?

744
00:50:03,900 --> 00:50:06,980
Yeah, the bridge opened up like it was cheering
"banzai,"

745
00:50:06,980 --> 00:50:09,960
and a big ship would pass right under it.

746
00:50:10,880 --> 00:50:14,320
That bridge was known as the big shot of the Sumida River,
you know.

747
00:50:14,320 --> 00:50:18,640
Well, there's no point telling you this
kind of story when you grew up in America.

748
00:50:19,260 --> 00:50:20,340
That's not true.

749
00:50:21,820 --> 00:50:23,880
I was born in this town too.

750
00:50:23,880 --> 00:50:26,580
My father was a fireworks craftsman.

751
00:50:27,580 --> 00:50:29,100
We were never well-off,

752
00:50:29,460 --> 00:50:31,920
but the three of us, Father,
Mother, and I, were happy.

753
00:50:32,720 --> 00:50:33,500
Well, I'm surprised.

754
00:50:33,980 --> 00:50:36,040
I didn't expect Lisa to
be born in the Shitamachi.

755
00:50:37,900 --> 00:50:39,560
Every day, playing with the boys,

756
00:50:40,100 --> 00:50:42,360
I'd play with rice-sesame
balls and silver-ball toy guns.

757
00:50:43,280 --> 00:50:44,460
Covered head to toe in mud.

758
00:50:45,260 --> 00:50:45,760
Why?

759
00:50:46,060 --> 00:50:47,540
Well, that's just like us, isn't it?

760
00:50:48,460 --> 00:50:50,080
We never missed the festivals,

761
00:50:51,360 --> 00:50:52,200
watching the souvenir fireworks.

762
00:50:53,040 --> 00:50:54,700
Those were the happiest days, weren't they?

763
00:50:55,120 --> 00:50:57,880
So that means I was watching
those same fireworks too

764
00:50:58,460 --> 00:51:00,400
How's your father doing?

765
00:51:03,660 --> 00:51:06,140
My father was swindled by a bad contractor,

766
00:51:06,800 --> 00:51:09,440
and to pay off the debt, he was made to
work through the night for days on end.

767
00:51:12,060 --> 00:51:13,880
And then,
on the night before the fireworks festival,

768
00:51:29,200 --> 00:51:32,200
So she was taken in by her
mother's relatives in America.

769
00:51:33,880 --> 00:51:35,680
But she was far from happy.

770
00:51:37,180 --> 00:51:39,960
You had a hard time too,
didn't you, despite how you look.

771
00:51:41,980 --> 00:51:44,560
But I love this town the most in the world.

772
00:51:45,440 --> 00:51:47,740
I also have memories that
make my heart flutter.

773
00:51:48,240 --> 00:51:49,660
Reiko's first love?

774
00:51:49,980 --> 00:51:51,840
A good man like me, right?

775
00:51:52,680 --> 00:51:54,780
Sorry, but he's someone much more wonderful.

776
00:51:54,780 --> 00:51:56,680
Who the hell is that?

777
00:51:56,680 --> 00:51:58,160
You don't even know his name?

778
00:51:59,240 --> 00:52:02,300
But to me, he looked like a prince.

779
00:52:08,720 --> 00:52:11,140
Come on, don't cry now.

780
00:52:11,800 --> 00:52:14,720
The god of happiness hates crybabies.

781
00:52:15,460 --> 00:52:18,480
If you keep crying,
you won't be able to find your treasure.

782
00:52:20,900 --> 00:52:22,020
I won't cry anymore.

783
00:52:26,260 --> 00:52:28,240
Hey, what kind of memories were they?

784
00:52:28,240 --> 00:52:29,820
Let me hear them too.

785
00:52:29,820 --> 00:52:32,960
No way,
my precious memories would get tainted.

786
00:52:33,540 --> 00:52:36,440
Hey, you're calling me a germ or something!

787
00:52:37,460 --> 00:52:41,080
I want to protect this town,
which is full of my memories.

788
00:52:42,540 --> 00:52:43,740
Is it from Benten Kozo?

789
00:52:45,620 --> 00:52:48,460
Benten Kozo won't show up anymore.

790
00:52:49,740 --> 00:52:53,580
Anyway, those memories from
back then are my treasure.

791
00:52:55,140 --> 00:52:57,080
Memories are treasure

792
00:53:00,120 --> 00:53:01,440
We found the treasure!

793
00:53:02,160 --> 00:53:04,940
We did it! We did it, we did it, we did it!

794
00:53:05,220 --> 00:53:08,780
Tonight we feast! All-you-can-eat yakiniku!

795
00:53:08,800 --> 00:53:12,140
Boss! Take us to a hostess
club afterward, please!

796
00:53:12,500 --> 00:53:14,800
I'll buy the whole hostess club, no problem!

797
00:53:16,520 --> 00:53:19,000
That's the buried gold
I've been searching for!

798
00:53:19,900 --> 00:53:20,620
Hey!

799
00:53:25,700 --> 00:53:27,020
Are you okay? Ryo-chan, Boss?

800
00:53:27,420 --> 00:53:29,180
Ow ow ow ow ow ow

801
00:53:29,180 --> 00:53:31,400
Falling into a hole you dug yourself...

802
00:53:31,400 --> 00:53:35,140
Damn it! What was all that hard work for?!

803
00:53:45,180 --> 00:53:46,400
Ryo-chan, you ready?

804
00:53:47,020 --> 00:53:48,700
Reiko, what's up?

805
00:53:49,780 --> 00:53:52,020
I have something I want to talk to you about,
Ryo-chan.

806
00:53:52,460 --> 00:53:53,260
Something to talk about?

807
00:53:53,860 --> 00:53:55,880
I looked into Lisa-san.

808
00:53:56,340 --> 00:53:58,400
And it turns out Lisa-san's parents

809
00:53:58,400 --> 00:54:01,840
died twenty years ago in
a firework factory accident.

810
00:54:02,340 --> 00:54:03,160
I know.

811
00:54:03,580 --> 00:54:06,120
They were working themselves to
the bone to pay off debts, right?

812
00:54:06,740 --> 00:54:08,400
The one who caused that

813
00:54:08,400 --> 00:54:10,720
was Sinatra's finance company.

814
00:54:11,100 --> 00:54:11,700
What?

815
00:54:11,700 --> 00:54:12,960
For Lisa-san,

816
00:54:12,960 --> 00:54:15,920
Sinatra is the enemy who killed her parents.

817
00:54:16,360 --> 00:54:17,380
So that's how it is.

818
00:54:17,900 --> 00:54:19,860
What do you think, Ryo-chan?

819
00:54:20,400 --> 00:54:21,120
What do you mean?

820
00:54:21,120 --> 00:54:23,580
Don't tell me you're...

821
00:54:24,980 --> 00:54:28,060
Benten Kozo won't show up again

822
00:54:31,180 --> 00:54:35,940
Lisa is the real Benten, Ryo-chan.

823
00:55:02,980 --> 00:55:03,940
Lisa

824
00:55:16,160 --> 00:55:18,360
I wanted to protect the treasure.

825
00:55:19,220 --> 00:55:20,260
That's all it was.

826
00:55:21,880 --> 00:55:23,240
Even now, twenty years later,

827
00:55:23,840 --> 00:55:25,960
Sinatra is tormenting
the people of this town.

828
00:55:26,900 --> 00:55:28,480
taking away the children's playground,

829
00:55:28,900 --> 00:55:31,220
exposing the residents to
the danger of mass death,

830
00:55:31,700 --> 00:55:33,360
doing whatever they please.

831
00:55:34,160 --> 00:55:35,000
When I learned that,

832
00:55:35,640 --> 00:55:37,680
the anger I had nearly
forgotten came flooding back.

833
00:55:38,420 --> 00:55:38,740
So,

834
00:55:39,420 --> 00:55:39,860
Lisa

835
00:55:40,500 --> 00:55:42,880
Think back to your father's fireworks.

836
00:55:44,180 --> 00:55:46,560
Your father's fireworks
brought joy to everyone,

837
00:55:46,560 --> 00:55:48,220
made people happy.

838
00:55:49,060 --> 00:55:50,700
But bombs aren't like that.

839
00:55:51,080 --> 00:55:54,880
Even with the same gunpowder,
they bring suffering and harm to people.

840
00:55:56,100 --> 00:55:57,860
Even if it's to protect the town,

841
00:55:57,860 --> 00:56:00,240
no one is happy about bombs.

842
00:56:00,680 --> 00:56:03,060
Your father surely thinks so too.

843
00:56:04,220 --> 00:56:05,760
Yes, I was wrong.

844
00:56:06,460 --> 00:56:09,920
I almost dragged even a small child into it.

845
00:56:10,920 --> 00:56:11,520
Lisa.

846
00:56:13,240 --> 00:56:15,120
Come on, arrest me.

847
00:56:16,080 --> 00:56:17,220
There's no need for that.

848
00:56:19,360 --> 00:56:21,580
Benten Kozo won't appear again.

849
00:56:21,580 --> 00:56:23,240
You said that, didn't you?

850
00:56:24,680 --> 00:56:25,180
Yes.

851
00:56:26,340 --> 00:56:28,560
If that's true, then that's enough.

852
00:56:32,320 --> 00:56:33,580
Corporal Ryotsu.

853
00:56:49,880 --> 00:56:56,820
Sinatra Shokai, whose tax evasion and unlicensed
grave-visit processing have come to light one after another,

854
00:56:56,820 --> 00:57:00,940
faces residents' eviction protests
that are growing ever more heated.

855
00:57:01,940 --> 00:57:05,520
Mr. Goike,
what do you think of Sinatra Shokai?

856
00:57:06,020 --> 00:57:10,640
Putting up a building that tall,
even the bonsai have withered away!

857
00:57:11,080 --> 00:57:14,240
It was supposed to be a nursing home,
you know!

858
00:57:15,620 --> 00:57:19,340
Complaints like these keep
pouring in from the site as well.

859
00:57:19,680 --> 00:57:21,080
This has been a report from the scene.

860
00:57:21,680 --> 00:57:24,160
Hey, miss,
won't you give me your phone number?

861
00:57:24,160 --> 00:57:27,240
Despite fierce opposition
from the local community,

862
00:57:27,240 --> 00:57:32,560
Sinatra Shokai is reportedly
preparing to launch some new project.

863
00:57:35,420 --> 00:57:40,660
Damn, with all this uproar, building
Sinatra World is getting harder, isn't it?

864
00:57:41,460 --> 00:57:44,900
Compared to that,
Benten Kozo is apparently hugely popular.

865
00:57:45,420 --> 00:57:45,780
What?

866
00:57:46,600 --> 00:57:49,220
Benten Kozo senbei, Benten Kozo dorayaki,

867
00:57:49,220 --> 00:57:51,960
and on top of that,
Benten-chan curry and Benten-chan furikake.

868
00:57:51,960 --> 00:57:54,960
They're even releasing Benten-chan
strawberry daifuku, I hear.

869
00:57:55,920 --> 00:57:58,760
Should we jump on the bandwagon
and make some money too?

870
00:57:59,480 --> 00:58:01,800
Don't be ridiculous! What's with this
"Benten-chan" nonsense!

871
00:58:02,400 --> 00:58:03,600
Wait a minute...

872
00:58:04,100 --> 00:58:04,820
President.

873
00:58:04,820 --> 00:58:06,980
You're right, just as you said.

874
00:58:06,980 --> 00:58:09,440
This guy might be useful after all.

875
00:58:15,840 --> 00:58:19,520
My two-week suspension is over,
so I'll do my best again.

876
00:58:19,520 --> 00:58:22,560
What are you going on about so carelessly?

877
00:58:22,560 --> 00:58:25,140
It's another message from Benten Kozo.

878
00:58:26,080 --> 00:58:27,240
From Benten Kozo?

879
00:58:27,940 --> 00:58:28,340
Who?

880
00:58:32,700 --> 00:58:36,520
The finest theme park in the Orient,
due for completion next year.

881
00:58:36,520 --> 00:58:39,940
Destroy Sinatra World's symbolic rocket?

882
00:58:40,480 --> 00:58:41,520
Benten Kozo?

883
00:58:42,980 --> 00:58:45,620
It sounds like an
advertisement for a theme park.

884
00:58:45,620 --> 00:58:48,640
Chief, this has to be a fake.

885
00:58:49,020 --> 00:58:49,700
A fake.

886
00:58:49,700 --> 00:58:54,520
Now that you mention it,
the Benten Kozo mark does look a bit off.

887
00:58:55,500 --> 00:58:57,760
Anyway, everyone,
gather at the investigation headquarters!

888
00:59:04,480 --> 00:59:07,880
Thank you all for coming here today.

889
00:59:07,880 --> 00:59:08,320
Thank you very much.

890
00:59:09,340 --> 00:59:12,900
How could anyone destroy Sinatra World,
our dream paradise?

891
00:59:12,900 --> 00:59:14,760
We will never forgive that.

892
00:59:15,280 --> 00:59:17,860
We are Asia's number one theme park,

893
00:59:17,860 --> 00:59:20,680
and in order to complete Sinatra World,

894
00:59:20,680 --> 00:59:24,800
we declare that we will
fight the utterly evil Benten.

895
00:59:25,380 --> 00:59:28,620
1, 2, 1, 2, 3, 4

896
00:59:28,620 --> 00:59:31,920
Sinatra World is

897
00:59:32,940 --> 00:59:35,600
Our spirit will never lose.

898
00:59:35,600 --> 00:59:37,580
Make sure to show it properly, okay?

899
00:59:37,580 --> 00:59:41,240
And don't forget the
Sinatra World sign behind you.

900
00:59:44,620 --> 00:59:46,320
Damn that Sinatra!

901
00:59:46,320 --> 00:59:48,940
He's using Benten Kozo for publicity,
isn't he?

902
00:59:49,480 --> 00:59:50,320
That's awful!

903
00:59:50,320 --> 00:59:54,020
The real Benten Kozo would
never do something like this!

904
00:59:54,740 --> 00:59:58,140
You two sure are taking Benten Kozo's side,
aren't you?

905
00:59:58,860 --> 01:00:00,360
That's not it, though.

906
01:00:01,240 --> 01:00:03,600
But that stingy Sinatra
would go out of his way to

907
01:00:05,600 --> 01:00:09,160
go to such lengths... I've heard
Sinatra took out a huge insurance policy.

908
01:00:09,560 --> 01:00:15,880
Even if people get conned, it's a scheme that still makes money, right?
Damn it, we won't let them get their way!

909
01:00:16,360 --> 01:00:22,360
That senpai would really go and do that...
What a hopeless guy, Lisa-san.

910
01:00:22,980 --> 01:00:28,420
No, I don't think so.
Either way, we can't let Ryotsu go alone.

911
01:00:28,860 --> 01:00:30,500
We're rushing to the scene too!

912
01:00:44,560 --> 01:00:46,100
Only three hours left

913
01:00:46,560 --> 01:00:49,140
The bomb's properly planted, right?

914
01:00:49,140 --> 01:00:50,740
Don't worry about it.

915
01:00:51,180 --> 01:00:55,060
We're using a surplus missile from the former Soviet military,
just as it is.

916
01:00:56,820 --> 01:00:58,340
So, how good is it?

917
01:00:58,700 --> 01:01:01,380
I think it's a 2,000-pound
bomb or something.

918
01:01:01,380 --> 01:01:02,660
2,000 pounds!

919
01:01:02,660 --> 01:01:02,720
How about that?

920
01:01:03,020 --> 01:01:03,660
Gaah!

921
01:01:03,660 --> 01:01:05,380
After all, we've got health insurance.

922
01:01:05,380 --> 01:01:06,700
We've got to go big, right?

923
01:01:07,200 --> 01:01:08,660
Boss?

924
01:01:09,380 --> 01:01:10,820
You!

925
01:01:11,360 --> 01:01:12,640
If it's 2,000 pounds...

926
01:01:12,640 --> 01:01:14,360
It's a ton!

927
01:01:14,360 --> 01:01:15,640
A ton!?

928
01:01:15,640 --> 01:01:17,960
Wasn't it supposed to be just 1 kilo!?

929
01:01:17,960 --> 01:01:19,700
Not just Sinatra World,

930
01:01:19,700 --> 01:01:21,140
the whole town's going to be blown away!

931
01:01:21,340 --> 01:01:22,660
Yeah!

932
01:01:23,080 --> 01:01:24,300
W-what do we do!

933
01:01:29,740 --> 01:01:31,720
Now I've gotta get out of here fast!

934
01:01:33,860 --> 01:01:35,220
Ah ah!

935
01:01:35,220 --> 01:01:36,400
Hey, Ishida Toro!

936
01:01:37,200 --> 01:01:40,700
You bastards, posing as Benten Kozo,
what the hell are you scheming?!

937
01:01:41,420 --> 01:01:42,580
I'll drive.

938
01:01:43,240 --> 01:01:45,000
Like I said, you drive!

939
01:01:45,220 --> 01:01:47,840
Hey, hey! Are you listening to this?!

940
01:01:48,020 --> 01:01:50,140
I don't have time to
talk to the likes of you!

941
01:01:50,300 --> 01:01:52,500
Hey damn it!

942
01:01:52,860 --> 01:01:54,600
Hold it! I'm not letting you get away!

943
01:01:54,840 --> 01:01:55,340
Yaaah!

944
01:01:56,100 --> 01:01:57,660
Hey! Over there!

945
01:01:58,000 --> 01:01:59,900
It's about to go off!
We'll all be blown sky-high!

946
01:01:59,900 --> 01:02:03,200
What? A single bomb has been planted!

947
01:02:03,820 --> 01:02:04,400
What?!

948
01:02:05,320 --> 01:02:06,040
Ryotsu!

949
01:02:06,160 --> 01:02:09,440
Chief! I knew it,
these guys planted the bomb!

950
01:02:09,840 --> 01:02:12,000
This isn't Benten Kozo's doing!

951
01:02:12,960 --> 01:02:14,820
What? Everyone, catch them!

952
01:02:18,980 --> 01:02:19,940
Let's do this!

953
01:02:26,140 --> 01:02:28,980
Idiots! Run, quickly!

954
01:02:37,120 --> 01:02:39,040
The rocket's in danger! Run!

955
01:02:50,400 --> 01:02:52,600
I can't believe it fell over so easily.

956
01:02:53,140 --> 01:02:54,440
What a huge cave-in.

957
01:02:54,440 --> 01:02:57,100
So they were doing shoddy construction work.

958
01:03:03,020 --> 01:03:05,080
The Benten Kozo message is a fake.

959
01:03:05,580 --> 01:03:08,140
Benten Kozo can't possibly
commit any more incidents.

960
01:03:09,520 --> 01:03:11,400
What exactly do you mean by that?

961
01:03:12,400 --> 01:03:14,640
The truth is,
Benten Kozo's true identity is...

962
01:03:15,200 --> 01:03:16,440
Chief, it's serious!

963
01:03:16,440 --> 01:03:19,720
Sinatra World's rocket
has collapsed underground.

964
01:03:19,720 --> 01:03:20,280
What?

965
01:03:20,900 --> 01:03:25,640
A high-performance one-ton bomb is
going to explode in just three hours!

966
01:03:26,260 --> 01:03:27,060
What did you just say?!

967
01:03:32,440 --> 01:03:36,620
A large bomb may explode in three hours.

968
01:03:37,440 --> 01:03:41,360
All Katsushika residents,
please evacuate immediately.

969
01:03:43,860 --> 01:03:47,800
Residents of Katsushika,
there are three hours until the explosion.

970
01:03:48,440 --> 01:03:51,860
Please follow the police
guidance and evacuate promptly.

971
01:03:51,860 --> 01:03:52,020
Yes.

972
01:03:57,980 --> 01:04:00,480
This is a terrible situation, President.

973
01:04:00,480 --> 01:04:03,300
It's because you planted a
first-class bomb like that!

974
01:04:03,480 --> 01:04:05,140
I'm terribly sorry.

975
01:04:05,140 --> 01:04:07,360
Hurry and get the jet ready!

976
01:04:07,360 --> 01:04:09,600
Ah, mosha mosha.

977
01:04:09,600 --> 01:04:10,160
Hmph.

978
01:04:25,360 --> 01:04:28,360
Evacuation orders have been
issued for all of Katsushika Ward.

979
01:04:28,360 --> 01:04:31,560
Anyone still remaining,
please evacuate immediately.

980
01:04:32,360 --> 01:04:33,920
There isn't a single person left.

981
01:04:33,920 --> 01:04:36,180
Looks like humanity has been wiped out.

982
01:04:37,840 --> 01:04:41,820
The explosive with an ignition device
that fell into the underground cavity

983
01:04:42,460 --> 01:04:45,920
turned out to be a modified
Soviet-era R2 missile.

984
01:04:46,700 --> 01:04:49,320
The warhead holds 2,000 pounds
of conventional explosives.

985
01:04:50,040 --> 01:04:52,094
Based on this information,
the predicted outcome is as follows.

986
01:04:52,144 --> 01:04:55,000
This is the area that will suffer
direct damage from the explosion.

987
01:04:55,000 --> 01:04:57,210
Then there's secondary damage,
such as ground subsidence,

988
01:04:57,260 --> 01:05:01,180
and tertiary damage, where lifelines like electricity are cut.
This is it.

989
01:05:02,540 --> 01:05:05,280
H-how do we even dispose of this bomb?

990
01:05:05,960 --> 01:05:08,033
First, we stop the dimensional device,

991
01:05:08,083 --> 01:05:11,340
then we have no choice but to
quickly move it to a safe place.

992
01:05:11,940 --> 01:05:14,908
But if disarming the
dimensional device takes too long,

993
01:05:14,958 --> 01:05:17,500
we won't have time to
run back to a safe place.

994
01:05:20,020 --> 01:05:24,320
This is far more dangerous than
any of Benten Kozo's previous bombs.

995
01:05:24,760 --> 01:05:26,940
It's a literal life-or-death job.

996
01:05:27,560 --> 01:05:28,380
This is bad!

997
01:05:29,320 --> 01:05:30,780
Liza and Dandy aren't here!

998
01:05:31,160 --> 01:05:32,800
Looks like they headed to
the scene by helicopter.

999
01:05:32,800 --> 01:05:33,440
What?

1000
01:05:49,560 --> 01:05:51,240
Dandy, let's go.

1001
01:05:52,200 --> 01:05:52,840
Roger.

1002
01:05:56,620 --> 01:05:57,380
Wait a minute!

1003
01:05:59,900 --> 01:06:03,380
I'm coming too!
I'm not letting them wreck this town!

1004
01:06:04,220 --> 01:06:06,560
Officer Ryotsu, when did you get here?

1005
01:06:07,220 --> 01:06:10,160
Hanging off the helicopter
is my usual spot, right?

1006
01:06:10,780 --> 01:06:13,840
Did you forget? We're a team!

1007
01:06:18,060 --> 01:06:18,470
Chief,

1008
01:06:18,520 --> 01:06:22,820
Reiko, Dandy, and I are heading
out now to defuse the bomb.

1009
01:06:23,520 --> 01:06:24,620
W-what?!

1010
01:06:25,280 --> 01:06:26,080
Senpai...

1011
01:06:26,080 --> 01:06:27,080
Ryo-chan...

1012
01:06:27,080 --> 01:06:27,778
Ryotsu,

1013
01:06:27,828 --> 01:06:31,420
Do you have any idea how
dangerous that bomb is!?

1014
01:06:31,420 --> 01:06:34,520
We know! Just leave it to us!

1015
01:06:35,120 --> 01:06:36,500
Reiko, Dandy, let's go!

1016
01:06:36,980 --> 01:06:37,300
Yes!

1017
01:06:39,280 --> 01:06:43,000
Ohara-kun, we have no choice but
to leave it to Ryotsu and Reiko.

1018
01:06:43,900 --> 01:06:44,220
Yes.

1019
01:06:55,320 --> 01:06:58,100
It's a spinning top.
Someone must've dropped it.

1020
01:06:59,240 --> 01:07:03,300
Will children be able to play with
spinning tops in this town again?

1021
01:07:03,960 --> 01:07:05,540
They will. Absolutely.

1022
01:07:12,760 --> 01:07:16,980
Apparently, the Katsushika police have
dispatched their explosives disposal unit.

1023
01:07:17,980 --> 01:07:21,620
If that high-performance bomb explodes,
the damage beyond that is incalculable!

1024
01:07:22,020 --> 01:07:24,880
Can the explosion really be avoided?

1025
01:07:34,860 --> 01:07:35,600
There!

1026
01:07:55,000 --> 01:07:56,340
Aaaaaaa

1027
01:07:56,340 --> 01:07:56,960
Aaaaaaa

1028
01:07:58,780 --> 01:08:01,840
This is terrible, this is really terrible!

1029
01:08:02,360 --> 01:08:05,760
Chief! We'll be a little
late because of a landslide!

1030
01:08:05,900 --> 01:08:07,620
W-what?!

1031
01:08:18,620 --> 01:08:20,714
Dangie, once this mission is over,

1032
01:08:20,764 --> 01:08:22,640
I'm gonna scrub you clean in the bath,
you hear?

1033
01:08:23,720 --> 01:08:26,700
Promise, promise! Essaka, poisaka!

1034
01:08:26,700 --> 01:08:27,800
Yeah, I promise!

1035
01:08:28,420 --> 01:08:30,070
Essaka, poisaka,

1036
01:08:30,120 --> 01:08:32,500
Essaka, essaka, essaka!

1037
01:08:33,060 --> 01:08:35,560
You two look just like brothers.

1038
01:08:37,680 --> 01:08:40,351
It's taking too long. If we don't hurry,

1039
01:08:40,401 --> 01:08:42,820
even if we fail,
there won't be time to come back.

1040
01:08:46,300 --> 01:08:47,680
Going any further is dangerous.

1041
01:08:48,800 --> 01:08:52,120
Ryotsu, abort the bomb disposal!
Get back here now!

1042
01:08:52,120 --> 01:08:54,480
Chief, I'm going on ahead.

1043
01:08:55,020 --> 01:08:55,380
What?

1044
01:08:56,180 --> 01:08:57,280
I'm going too.

1045
01:08:57,720 --> 01:08:58,240
Reiko.

1046
01:08:59,540 --> 01:09:02,480
We're a team, Senior Officer Ryotsu.

1047
01:09:05,460 --> 01:09:10,040
Lisa, what's gotten into you too?
Don't you understand it's dangerous?

1048
01:09:10,580 --> 01:09:12,680
If you don't come back right away,
you'll lose your lives!

1049
01:09:13,380 --> 01:09:14,620
Hey! Ryotsu! Ryotsu!

1050
01:09:15,200 --> 01:09:17,140
There's no time left to turn back.

1051
01:09:17,960 --> 01:09:21,300
If we can't stop the dimensional device...

1052
01:09:22,220 --> 01:09:23,080
Senpai...

1053
01:09:23,500 --> 01:09:24,640
Ryo-chan...

1054
01:09:31,080 --> 01:09:32,180
Alright, we're here!

1055
01:09:32,800 --> 01:09:34,760
That window over there, it's fine.

1056
01:09:35,160 --> 01:09:36,640
If it's Dangie, he'll pull it off.

1057
01:10:01,380 --> 01:10:02,680
Dangie

1058
01:10:02,680 --> 01:10:05,260
Hey, Dangie, hang in there!

1059
01:10:05,260 --> 01:10:06,260
Dangie

1060
01:10:06,260 --> 01:10:06,940
Yassa

1061
01:10:06,940 --> 01:10:08,540
Yassa

1062
01:10:08,540 --> 01:10:09,780
Yassa

1063
01:10:09,780 --> 01:10:10,680
Ya -

1064
01:10:10,680 --> 01:10:13,460
Dangie

1065
01:10:19,600 --> 01:10:20,540
Dangie!

1066
01:10:24,360 --> 01:10:25,240
This guy

1067
01:10:25,680 --> 01:10:27,520
He did this to save me.

1068
01:10:28,660 --> 01:10:29,520
Sorry, buddy.

1069
01:10:30,420 --> 01:10:33,260
I promised to scrub you clean,
and now look at you.

1070
01:10:34,280 --> 01:10:35,960
Dangie!

1071
01:10:37,340 --> 01:10:37,900
Lisa

1072
01:10:38,360 --> 01:10:39,680
We don't have time to cry.

1073
01:10:39,680 --> 01:10:40,380
Yeah.

1074
01:10:45,300 --> 01:10:47,580
Only five minutes left!

1075
01:10:48,540 --> 01:10:50,700
This is a tough dimensional device,
you know.

1076
01:10:51,120 --> 01:10:52,460
If we just cut the lead wire,

1077
01:10:55,680 --> 01:10:56,600
I can't reach it.

1078
01:10:58,000 --> 01:11:00,220
We only need to cut that red cord.

1079
01:11:01,420 --> 01:11:03,560
My arms are too short for this.

1080
01:11:04,840 --> 01:11:06,100
If only Dangie were here.

1081
01:11:08,760 --> 01:11:09,880
Three minutes left.

1082
01:11:09,880 --> 01:11:11,120
What? No way.

1083
01:11:11,120 --> 01:11:11,700
No way!

1084
01:11:12,120 --> 01:11:15,340
Ryotsu, please do your best!

1085
01:11:18,260 --> 01:11:19,140
Ryo-chan!

1086
01:11:20,100 --> 01:11:22,775
Be careful.
If you cut any other colored cord,

1087
01:11:22,825 --> 01:11:24,260
it'll explode right away.

1088
01:11:27,940 --> 01:11:30,420
Damn, I'm so close.

1089
01:11:32,700 --> 01:11:33,540
One minute left.

1090
01:11:34,060 --> 01:11:35,040
It's no use.

1091
01:11:35,240 --> 01:11:36,820
Liza, don't give up!

1092
01:11:37,140 --> 01:11:37,760
But...

1093
01:11:38,200 --> 01:11:41,620
I'm not giving up! We'll keep
fighting until the very last second!

1094
01:11:42,320 --> 01:11:43,300
Ow

1095
01:11:43,800 --> 01:11:44,680
What's wrong?

1096
01:11:44,760 --> 01:11:45,680
Something stabbed me!

1097
01:11:48,000 --> 01:11:49,580
It's that piece from earlier...

1098
01:11:50,360 --> 01:11:52,780
That's it! This might fix things!

1099
01:11:53,560 --> 01:11:54,400
A piece?

1100
01:11:54,880 --> 01:11:58,000
Joats! This is no time
to be playing with pieces!

1101
01:11:58,880 --> 01:12:01,000
Thirty seconds left, senpai!

1102
01:12:06,860 --> 01:12:07,980
It's slipping off again.

1103
01:12:07,980 --> 01:12:08,960
Damn it!

1104
01:12:16,540 --> 01:12:17,200
Hurry!

1105
01:12:39,500 --> 01:12:41,440
Yes!

1106
01:12:48,840 --> 01:12:51,040
What's wrong, Ryotsu?

1107
01:12:51,040 --> 01:12:53,700
Hey, answer me!

1108
01:12:53,700 --> 01:12:57,100
Ryotsu! Ryotsu! Ryotsu!

1109
01:13:00,340 --> 01:13:03,320
Chief! Chief!

1110
01:13:03,320 --> 01:13:05,900
Ryotsu!

1111
01:13:06,920 --> 01:13:07,940
Are you all right?

1112
01:13:08,260 --> 01:13:12,640
Yes! The rocket that was sticking
out of the tunnel just fell inside!

1113
01:13:12,760 --> 01:13:17,300
The detonator is completely stopped!
The mission is complete!

1114
01:13:18,180 --> 01:13:19,120
Yes!

1115
01:13:20,380 --> 01:13:21,360
Ryotsu!

1116
01:13:21,780 --> 01:13:24,580
Senpai! Ryotsu did it perfectly!

1117
01:13:24,920 --> 01:13:28,160
Well done!
You really came through for Katsushika!

1118
01:13:28,960 --> 01:13:32,720
Ryotsu!
I'm absolutely overwhelmed right now!

1119
01:13:33,720 --> 01:13:36,340
Banzai! Banzai! Banzai!

1120
01:13:36,340 --> 01:13:40,760
Banzai! Banzai! Banzai!

1121
01:13:40,780 --> 01:13:42,960
Banzai! Banzai! Banzai!

1122
01:13:42,960 --> 01:13:44,060
Banzai! Banzai!

1123
01:13:44,060 --> 01:13:45,880
We did it, Reiko.

1124
01:13:45,880 --> 01:13:48,820
Ryo-san

1125
01:13:48,820 --> 01:13:50,300
Ryo-san

