1289
01:24:38,060 --> 01:24:40,000
We'll set it off safely in the air!

1290
01:24:40,380 --> 01:24:41,020
Yes!

1291
01:24:48,740 --> 01:24:50,220
That mid-air explosion just now!

1292
01:24:50,500 --> 01:24:52,000
I'm brilliant, if I do say so myself!

1293
01:24:56,460 --> 01:24:57,640
The cord snapped!

1294
01:24:58,040 --> 01:24:59,240
What do we do!

1295
01:25:02,000 --> 01:25:02,480
That's...!

1296
01:25:04,640 --> 01:25:06,740
The jet-ghee from the Sinatro introduction!

1297
01:25:07,100 --> 01:25:08,260
Let's roll it!

1298
01:25:13,800 --> 01:25:16,380
Looks like we managed to stop the explosion.

1299
01:25:17,760 --> 01:25:20,260
I have no use for a city
full of fools like this.

1300
01:25:23,160 --> 01:25:23,740
Noa!

1301
01:25:46,380 --> 01:25:47,700
Aaaaaaah!

1302
01:25:49,300 --> 01:25:50,340
Aaaaaaah!

1303
01:25:50,340 --> 01:25:52,460
Aaaaaaah!

1304
01:25:52,460 --> 01:25:52,720
Aaaaaaah!

1305
01:26:06,060 --> 01:26:09,780
But blowing itself up...
what a fairly stupid thing to do.

1306
01:27:03,340 --> 01:27:06,680
So you're really being deported after all,
Lisa-san.

1307
01:27:06,680 --> 01:27:09,400
Whatever the reason, a crime is a crime.

1308
01:27:09,400 --> 01:27:12,960
But thanks to you, Lisa-san,
we were able to arrest Shinatara.

1309
01:27:12,960 --> 01:27:15,160
I wish something could be done about it.

1310
01:27:16,280 --> 01:27:18,460
Your pickup should be arriving soon.

1311
01:27:25,140 --> 01:27:27,680
Wow, it's a real Harrier!

1312
01:27:27,680 --> 01:27:29,300
It belongs to my father's company.

1313
01:27:34,020 --> 01:27:36,740
It's a shame, saying goodbye like this.

1314
01:27:36,740 --> 01:27:38,034
It can't be helped,

1315
01:27:38,084 --> 01:27:41,540
an FBI agent committed a crime, after all.

1316
01:27:47,000 --> 01:27:49,780
But it was Lisa who saved this town, too.

1317
01:27:51,340 --> 01:27:54,100
It wasn't me, it was Ryo-san.

1318
01:27:54,600 --> 01:27:56,780
Stop it, you're making me blush.

1319
01:27:59,680 --> 01:28:02,200
Ryo-san, thanks for everything.

1320
01:28:03,780 --> 01:28:05,020
Yeah, take care of yourself.

1321
01:28:11,040 --> 01:28:13,320
Don't you cry, Lisa.

1322
01:28:14,160 --> 01:28:16,860
The god of happiness hates crybabies.

1323
01:28:33,820 --> 01:28:36,160
Come on, don't cry anymore.

1324
01:28:36,160 --> 01:28:39,540
The lucky card hates crybabies.

1325
01:28:41,160 --> 01:28:42,080
Ryo-san

1326
01:28:52,440 --> 01:28:54,520
It's going to be lonely, senpai.

1327
01:28:54,520 --> 01:28:56,280
We'll see each other again.

1328
01:28:56,780 --> 01:28:58,200
That's right, we'll definitely meet again.

1329
01:28:59,060 --> 01:29:02,080
I have a feeling we've
met somewhere before, too.

1330
01:29:05,400 --> 01:29:07,600
Dandy! He's back to normal!

1331
01:29:07,900 --> 01:29:09,520
Lisa fixed him before she left.

1332
01:29:09,980 --> 01:29:13,040
They said the most important part,
the memory, is fine.

1333
01:29:13,040 --> 01:29:15,680
I hear he's safely returning to the FBI.

1334
01:29:15,680 --> 01:29:17,960
Glad to hear it, Dandy!

1335
01:29:18,800 --> 01:29:20,280
Promise! Promise!

1336
01:29:20,440 --> 01:29:24,400
Dandy, as promised,
I'll scrub you clean in the bath.

1337
01:29:25,600 --> 01:29:26,040
Ryo-sama!

1338
01:29:27,620 --> 01:29:31,380
Ryo-sama! Are you all right?

1339
01:29:33,580 --> 01:29:34,558
Maria! You...

1340
01:29:34,608 --> 01:29:37,840
Weren't you supposed to
be in Hong Kong with Dad?

1341
01:29:38,120 --> 01:29:39,835
If it's for my future husband,

1342
01:29:39,885 --> 01:29:42,240
I'll rush to you from the ends of the earth!

1343
01:29:42,320 --> 01:29:44,060
Future husband? Whoa!

1344
01:29:48,540 --> 01:29:50,730
Because you're a man, you see,

1345
01:29:50,780 --> 01:29:53,820
I've told you, you can't marry me!

1346
01:29:55,400 --> 01:29:56,400
That's a dorky problem!

1347
01:29:56,640 --> 01:29:57,580
It's not dorky!

1348
01:30:04,300 --> 01:30:05,440
It's a mole!

1349
01:30:06,280 --> 01:30:08,380
I've told you, it's not a mole!

1350
01:30:08,900 --> 01:30:10,700
Just leave it alone, senpai.

1351
01:30:10,700 --> 01:30:13,060
Isn't it just a hole they
dug and left like that?

1352
01:30:24,520 --> 01:30:26,140
Yay!

1353
01:30:55,880 --> 01:31:02,380
It's a feeling, it's a feeling,
what I want to give you

1354
01:31:03,600 --> 01:31:10,440
It's a feeling,
it's a feeling, it's my feelings

1355
01:31:26,060 --> 01:31:41,600
If you shoulder heavy loads,
your hands will be free

1356
01:31:41,600 --> 01:31:49,460
If those hands could support someone

1357
01:31:50,100 --> 01:31:57,280
how wonderful that would be

1358
01:31:58,300 --> 01:32:02,580
It's a feeling, it's a feeling

1359
01:32:02,580 --> 01:32:04,920
what I want to give you

1360
01:32:06,020 --> 01:32:10,420
It's a feeling, it's a feeling

1361
01:32:37,080 --> 01:32:40,540
Thank you for watching.

1362
01:32:41,660 --> 01:32:44,360
There must be, surely.

1363
01:32:45,340 --> 01:32:51,860
It's a feeling, it's a feeling,
what I received from you

1364
01:32:52,760 --> 01:33:00,300
It's a feeling, it's a feeling,
it's your feelings

1365
01:33:03,000 --> 01:33:09,480
It's a feeling, it's a feeling,
what I want to give you

1366
01:33:10,800 --> 01:33:17,720
It's a feeling,
it's a feeling, it's my feelings

1367
01:33:18,600 --> 01:33:25,720
It's a feeling,
it's a feeling, it's my feelings

1368
01:33:58,540 --> 01:34:06,000
Thank you for watching.

